***REMOVED*** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
***REMOVED*** Proxmox CSI plugin credentials. A kubeconfig-style `config.yaml` pointing the
***REMOVED*** CSI controller at your Proxmox API. Copy to `proxmox-csi-secret.yaml`, fill
***REMOVED*** in. ArgoCD manages it.
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED***   cp proxmox-csi-secret.yaml.example proxmox-csi-secret.yaml
***REMOVED***   $EDITOR proxmox-csi-secret.yaml
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED*** The `config.yaml` value is the literal contents of the Proxmox CSI
***REMOVED*** configuration file (YAML-in-YAML; indent it under the block scalar). It holds
***REMOVED*** the Proxmox API URL, a token ID and token secret, and the node/fingerprint
***REMOVED*** mapping. See the proxmox-csi-plugin chart for the schema.
***REMOVED*** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
    name: proxmox-csi-plugin
    namespace: csi-proxmox
type: Opaque
stringData:
    config.yaml: |
        ***REMOVED*** ponytail: schema matches proxmox-csi-plugin; fill from your Proxmox API.
        clusters:
          - url: https://REPLACE_PROXMOX_API:8006
            insecure: false
            token_id: "REPLACE_TOKEN_ID"
            token_secret: "REPLACE_TOKEN_SECRET"
            region: REPLACE_REGION
